.TH GLIMT 1 "2026-10-12" "Glimt 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glimt \- fast, lightweight image viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glimt
.RI [ FILE_OR_FOLDER ]
.br
.B glimt
.B \-\-remote
.I COMMAND
.br
.B glimt
.B \-\-remote\-all
.I COMMAND
.br
.B glimt
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Glimt
shows the images of a folder, one at a time, with a file list beside them. It is inspired by
.BR geeqie (1)
and uses its keyboard shortcuts, but focuses on speed and little memory: the images on each
side of the shown one are decoded in advance at window size, and folders with hundreds of
thousands of files list as quickly as small ones.
.PP
Given a file, Glimt shows it with the rest of its folder; given a folder, its first image;
given nothing, the folder used last (if that is set in Preferences) or the current folder.
A URI such as
.I smb://server/share
is mounted with
.BR gio (1)
first.
.PP
It reads JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF (also animated), TIFF (also with several pages) and camera RAW
files by their embedded preview. Builds with optional features also read videos, HEIC, AVIF,
JPEG XL and SVG.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-remote " COMMAND"
Send
.I COMMAND
to the Glimt window used last.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-all " COMMAND"
Send
.I COMMAND
to every running Glimt.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
List the options and remote commands.
.SH REMOTE COMMANDS
.TP
.BR next ", " prev ", " first ", " last
Show the next, previous, first or last image.
.TP
.B slideshow
Start or stop the slideshow.
.TP
.B fullscreen
Enter or leave full screen.
.TP
.BI open " PATH"
Show a file or folder. If no Glimt is running, one is started.
.TP
.B quit
Close Glimt.
.SH KEYS
The keys are Geeqie's; Help \(-> Keyboard Shortcuts lists them all, and Preferences can change
them. The most used:
.TP
.BR Space ", " "Page Down" ", " \(->
Next image.
.TP
.BR Backspace ", " "Page Up" ", " \(<-
Previous image.
.TP
.BR Home ", " End
First and last image.
.TP
.BR Z ", " X ", " + ", " \-
Zoom 1:1, zoom to fit, zoom in and out.
.TP
.BR F ", " F11 ", " Esc
Enter and leave full screen.
.TP
.BR S ", " P ", " R
Start or stop the slideshow, pause it, random order.
.TP
.BR ] ", " [
Rotate the view clockwise and counterclockwise.
.TP
.B Delete
Move the selected files, or the shown one, to the trash.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Preferences.
.TP
.B F1
Help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/glimt/config
Preferences, as key=value lines (default
.IR ~/.config/glimt/config ).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/glimt/state
The last folder and the window size and position (default
.IR ~/.local/state/glimt/state ).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/glimt/marks
Marks and stars, in builds with the marks feature.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumbnails
Thumbnails, shared with other programs as the freedesktop specification says.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/glimt
The sockets for remote control.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME ", " XDG_CACHE_HOME ", " XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Where the files above are kept.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B glimt ~/Pictures
Show the images in ~/Pictures.
.TP
.B glimt \-\-remote next
Go to the next image in the Glimt used last, for example from a desktop shortcut.
.TP
.B glimt \-\-remote\-all quit
Close every Glimt.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR geeqie (1),
.BR gio (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.PP
https://github.com/thornbux/glimt
